      "body": "Purpose\r\nFixes #45317 — DSA models (GLM-5.1, DeepSeek-V3.2-family with use_sparse=True) fail to start on NVIDIA GB10/DGX Spark (SM121). The supports_compute_capability() method in FLASHMLA_SPARSE, FLASHMLA, and DeepSeekV4FlashMLA backends explicitly filters capability.major in [9, 10], excluding SM121 (major=12).\r\n\r\nTest Plan\r\nRun the capability check directly inside a DGX Spark container:bash\r\ndocker exec vllm-vl python3 -c \"\r\nfrom vllm.v1.attention.backends.mla.flashmla_sparse import FlashMLASparseBackend\r\nfrom vllm.v1.attention.backends.mla.flashmla import FlashMLABackend\r\nfrom vllm.platforms.interface import DeviceCapability\r\n\r\nsm121 = DeviceCapability(major=12, minor=1)\r\nprint('FLASHMLA_SPARSE SM121:', FlashMLASparseBackend.supports_compute_capability(sm121))\r\nprint('FLASHMLA SM121:', FlashMLABackend.supports_compute_capability(sm121))\r\n\"\r\nAfter patch: verify the same output returns True instead of False.\r\n\r\nTest Result\r\nEnvironment: NVIDIA GB10 (DGX Spark), CUDA 13.0, [nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm:26.03.post1-py3](http://nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm:26.03.post1-py3)--- BEFORE PATCH ---\r\nFLASHMLA_SPARSE SM121: False\r\nFLASHMLA SM121: False\r\n\r\n--- AFTER PATCH (added 12 to lists) ---\r\nFLASHMLA_SPARSE SM121: True\r\nFLASHMLA SM121: True\r\nThe FlashMLA kernels already support SM121 at the CMake level; only the Python capability gate was blocking selection.\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 3,
